  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between isocytisoside-7-O-glucoside and A-431 through a series of target interactions involving Raji cells. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence chains, all of which indicate that isocytisoside-7-O-glucoside acts as a target for Raji, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and terbutaline. These compounds are all linked to A-431, suggesting a possible mechanism of action where isocytisoside-7-O-glucoside may influence A-431 through the activation of Raji cells. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, highlighting a possible dependency on the target Raji for the interaction with A-431. The integration of these findings supports a mechanism where isocytisoside-7-O-glucoside may modulate A-431 via Raji, potentially through a shared biological pathway or a direct interaction at the Raji level.",
